answer:
According to Article 5.15 of the Collective Agreement 2016-2020, faculty members have the following Rights, Responsibilities and Duties:

"A) To conduct research and scholarship in their discipline;
B) To teach and deliver instruction in their field of expertise; 
C) to engage in service activities that contribute to the mission of the University and its academic programs;

Members are expected to uphold the norms of civil discourse, especially with regard to criticism, which in the academic setting is respectful, constructive, ad rem, reasonable, balanced, and fair in the use of evidence."

Source: LUFA-H Collective Agreement 2016-2020, Article 5.15

